HST Office: the open File panel keeps the keyboard when its window is activated again.

Writer gives the focus to its document view when its window is activated (Alt+Tab back, the task bar). The view
lies under the open File panel, so Esc, Ctrl+W and Ctrl+P went to it and did nothing; on the Print page, Ctrl+W
did not close the document as it does in Sheets. While the panel is open, a focus that goes to the view of its
frame is moved back to the panel's page after the activation (a posted event: the view takes it during the
activation). A click into the document still closes the panel first, as before.

- sfx2/source/backstage/hstbackstagewindow.cxx, sfx2/source/backstage/hstbackstagewindow.hxx (AppEventHdl,
  RefocusHdl, lcl_viewWindow).

License: these upstream-derived files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_backstage_panel_keeps_focus.py; tests/runtime/check-backstage-print-close.py (Windows: the
window activated again with the Print page open, then Esc closes the panel and Ctrl+W the document).

